# libvpx commit: 12f3a2ac603e8f10742105519e0cd03c3b8f71dd (v1.14.1)
# F.0.2 — per-block picker-decision oracle (HLD §3.3).
#
# Adds output-only instrumentation to `vp9_pick_inter_mode`, gated by
# `VPX_F02_ORACLE_OUT`. It emits the shared JSONL schema declared in
# `crates/rvp9-encoder/src/f02_oracle.rs`, including live LAST-reference
# candidate costs in `[ZERO, NEAREST, NEAR, NEW]` order and fresh NEWMV
# search start/full-pel/final stages. The independent
# `VPX_F02_MODEL_ORACLE_OUT` path captures a bounded sample of exact inputs
# and outputs for the regular luma model-RD function.
# `VPX_F02_BLOCK_YRD_ORACLE_OUT` captures bounded, non-skippable per-tile
# coefficient arrays and the corresponding `block_yrd` aggregate.
#
# The shared schema numbers skip-transform states as None=0, AcOnly=1,
# AcDc=2. libvpx's internal constants use None=0, AcDc=1, AcOnly=2, so
# this instrumentation normalises them before serialisation.
#
# Apply from `third_party/libvpx`:
#   git apply ../../third_party/libvpx-patches/f02_oracle.patch
#
